Some TPMs do. They need to have the encryptdecrypt command interface:

./tools/tpm2_getcap commands 2>/dev/null | grep -i encryptdecrypt
TPM2_CC_EncryptDecrypt:
TPM2_CC_EncryptDecrypt2:

If it doesn=E2=80=99t have that, you won't be able to generate symmetric ke=
ys AFAIK.
The only TPM I have heard has support in the wild is Intel PTT. But I could=
 be
wrong on that.

Bill


